  "body": "What happens: the release gate tier for the 0.19.0 cut is red in the app heavy lane (release, `--ignored`).\n`camcraft-app` test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` fails at `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:122`:\n\"the bore's path as the fix plans it: (16017, 15360, 1427)\".\n\nWhy: `bore_path_matches` pins the (moves, planar feeds, arcs) triple exactly per measured platform. PR #1376 (`8cd4c9188`, \"perf(adaptive): simplify growth outlines before opening\") re-measured macOS (16026, 15382, 1413) and Linux (16029, 15372, 1427), and its own comment says \"Windows remains its previously measured triple; this change still needs measurement there.\" Windows x86_64 still pins (16197, 15458, 1581). Measured on Windows now (release, tree `9047b5f6f` = main `38699549e` plus docs): (16017, 15360, 1427).\n\nEvery assertion before the triple passed in that run: no level falls back, no planning budget is reached, the op verifies clean. Only the pinned counts moved, and they sit beside the two re-measured platforms.\n\nEvidence: `gate-logs/release-20261113-113616/12-app_heavy_lane_release_--ignored_.log`. The suite is release-lane only (`#[ignore]`), so the quick and batch tiers never ran it.\n\nRerun: `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test pocket3d_hsm -- --ignored the_users_bore`\n\nDone means: the Windows triple is measured on current main in release, at least two runs identical, and pinned with a comment naming the measurement; the test passes; no other assertion in the test is loosened. If the runs differ, or an earlier assertion fails (a fallback level, a budget, verify not clean), that is a defect in the planner and is reported here instead of pinned.\n\nBlocks the 0.19.0 cut.\n",
